/**
 * @defgroup dl_modules Deep Learning Modules and Layers
 * @brief Core tensor/graph infrastructure, layers, optimizers, losses, and device backends --
 *        the building blocks every other group is composed from.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability Ad-hoc Interpretability
 * @brief Post-hoc explanation methods applied to an already-trained model, as opposed to
 *        the LRP relevance propagation built into each layer in @ref dl_modules.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability_agnostic Model-Agnostic
 * @ingroup interpretability
 * @brief Explainers that only need a model's input/output behavior (perturb-and-observe),
 *        with no access to gradients or internal activations.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability_dl Deep Learning Approaches
 * @ingroup interpretability
 * @brief Explainers that use a model's gradients, activations, or internal structure
 *        directly.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup rl Reinforcement Learning
 * @brief Environments, agents, and training algorithms (DQN, REINFORCE, A2C, PPO, SAC) built
 *        on the @ref dl_modules tensor/autograd core.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup mech_interp Mechanistic Interpretability
 * @brief Tools for inspecting and probing a model's internal computation directly --
 *        activation caching, linear probes, sparse autoencoders, circuit graphs -- plus the
 *        GFlowNet-based non-goal-directed training objectives motivated by the Scientist AI
 *        research direction.
 */
